'''areostyle, aræostyle''' (a-rē′ọ-stīl), ''a.'' [< L. ''aræostylos'', < Gr. ἀραιόστυλος, with columns far apart, < ἀραιός, thin, not dense, + στῦλος, a column, pillar: see ''style''<sup>2</sup>.] In ''arch.'', having columns placed four diameters, or more than three diameters, apart, from center to center of the columns.
